<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dairatul Maarifil Osmania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1888">1888</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Dairat al-Maarif al-Osmania</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dairatul Maarifil Osmania is a learned society and press in Hyderabad, founded in 1888 under the patronage of the Nizam, that edits and publishes classical Arabic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a>. Its editions of works of history, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadith">hadith</a>, medicine, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonian-astronomy">astronomy</a> and mathematics made many texts available for the first time. It has been attached to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osmania-university">Osmania University</a> since the mid-20th century.</p></div>
